            {
                "entry_id": "0f38a342-88bb-3f58-a154-8b175797d740",
                "word": "Archie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "046f2a37-bb3d-4067-a350-876e2de2b192",
                        "entry_id": "0f38a342-88bb-3f58-a154-8b175797d740",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Archies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a08e70ef-39b9-34dd-b26d-5b9459d529cc",
                        "entry_id": "0f38a342-88bb-3f58-a154-8b175797d740",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Anti-aircraft artillery."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "World-War-I",
                            "slang",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b7973dc7-154d-4fa7-a551-526e1cb6c01c",
                                "sense_id": "a08e70ef-39b9-34dd-b26d-5b9459d529cc",
                                "text": "But then, dodging airbursts of Archie on the Western Front hadn't exactly been a joyride either."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a00819d5-4633-4c33-8a34-6a156c53ac11",
                                "sense_id": "a08e70ef-39b9-34dd-b26d-5b9459d529cc",
                                "text": "He was seen by an aeroplane, our Archie gunner and a whole division to crash in their lines just opposite our trenches, much jubilation and more congratulations."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a354017b-431c-43f7-a395-80f6a1632e0a",
                                "sense_id": "a08e70ef-39b9-34dd-b26d-5b9459d529cc",
                                "text": "On a cloudy day one can hop in and out of the clouds, greatly to the annoyance of some Archie commander who, just when he has got range and direction and is about to let fly, finds that his bird has disappeared into a cloud. He fills thatcloud with HE but his quarry emerges from another nearby with a gesture of derision which the gunners below may imagine, though cannot see. On a sunny day, Archie is up early, for he knows that aircraft will be silhouetted against a blue sky. Then the experienced pilot hops in and out of the sun, there being no clouds, while the Archie commander rubs his smarting eyes and uses strong words."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5479ffa8-23c5-39d9-bc52-c3b07b1f3d74",
                        "entry_id": "0f38a342-88bb-3f58-a154-8b175797d740",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A piece of anti-aircraft ordnance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "World-War-I",
                            "countable",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "869a6d69-836a-4f9c-8793-dea4af0cb9f7",
                                "sense_id": "5479ffa8-23c5-39d9-bc52-c3b07b1f3d74",
                                "text": "An inquisitive aeroplane, which had been hovering over the scene, was picked off as by an Archie and made a forced landing, man and machine buried in filth."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6f3958c1-494f-4676-9cb4-bf59f55469ef",
                                "sense_id": "5479ffa8-23c5-39d9-bc52-c3b07b1f3d74",
                                "text": "Quickly our five machines dodged the Archies as we crossed."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "9e59e2f2-c5f5-3f6f-ae6f-ed47314e8df2",
                "word": "Archie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ad8b1b80-8ee6-4bc0-83a1-4e0de5f9acf8",
                        "entry_id": "9e59e2f2-c5f5-3f6f-ae6f-ed47314e8df2",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
